# USB_MUSB_HDRC/ARKMICRO must be built-in (=y), not module -- this is
# the USB host controller driver itself, and the "bootusb" boot mode
# (root=/dev/sda2, a USB stick, no initramfs) needs it available before
# root can ever be mounted, so it can never load as a module for that
# boot path. Was =m here (since the very first commit of this file)
# but had clearly been live-patched to =y in whatever .config actually
# produced every prior successful "new uboot new kernel baseline"
# log through v4 -- confirmed by musb-hdrc's own init lines appearing
# synchronously during early kernel boot in that log, well before
# "Waiting for root device", which only a built-in driver can do.
# 2026-07-19's --defconfig regeneration (for the ITU656/WiFi work --
# see the INET/WLAN comment above) silently reverted this back to the
# checked-in (wrong) =m default, causing baseline v5's hang at
