# CONFIG_ARK1668_ITU656 is not set -- reverted 2026-07-19, hard-disabled
# again after enabling it (linux-arkmicro 5f9fde926) caused a full kernel
# panic on every single boot, not just a failed camera feature.
# MsnCoreApp's arkapi_open_dvr() -> dvr_ioctl() reads a function pointer
# from dvr_dev->start/->stop (ark1668_itu656.h struct dvr_dev, fields at
# byte offset 0x200) and calls through it with only a non-NULL check --
# no other validation. dvr_dev is devm_kzalloc()'d (should be all-zero
# unless explicitly written), but at panic time that field held a
# non-NULL value that happened to decode to devm_kmalloc's real kernel
# address, called with garbage arguments -> NULL deref inside
# devm_kmalloc -> corrupted kernel stack -> panic. This is a real
# memory-corruption bug somewhere in ~2269 lines of decades-old vendor
# code (drivers/soc/arkmicro/itu656/ark1668_itu656.c), not something fixed
# by this config flag alone -- needs a dedicated Ghidra/source
# investigation to find what's actually corrupting that struct field
# before re-enabling. See docs/DEVICE_TEST_CHECKLIST_2026-07-18.md
# item 7 in the main repo for the full crash trace.
#
# RN6752 (I2C camera decoder chip driver) and ARK_CARBACK (reverse-gear
# integration, drivers/soc/arkmicro/ark-carback.c) turned out to also
# need disabling here -- both reference symbols
# (dvr_detect_carback_signal/dvr_enter_carback/dvr_exit_carback/
# dvr_get_pragressive/dvr_restart/dvr_exit_wait) defined only inside
# ark1668_itu656.c, so vmlinux fails to link with ITU656 off unless
# these are off too. They are NOT independently toggleable -- this
# whole group needs to be enabled or disabled together. RN6752's own
# probe (dvr_rn6752_probe) was safely succeeding on its own in every
# boot log before today (proving RN6752+ITU656+ARK_CARBACK were
# already silently enabled together in some past session's lost
# .config, same pattern as the INET/WLAN/MUSB regressions above) --
# the crash is specifically in ark1668_itu656.c's dvr_ioctl, not in
# rn6752.c or ark-carback.c themselves, but they can't be separated at
# link time as currently structured.
# CONFIG_ARK7116 is not set
# CONFIG_RN6752 is not set
# CONFIG_ARK_CARBACK is not set
# CONFIG_ARK_DISPLAY was also missing here -- discovered 2026-07-19
# when "open /dev/ark_display fail" started appearing repeatedly in
# MsnCoreApp's own log (baseline v7). Same INET/WLAN/MUSB/RN6752
